# Build context for backend/Dockerfile, which builds from the REPOSITORY ROOT
# because Tankbook.Api.csproj embeds ../../../docs/schemas/v1/*.schema.json.
#
# Written as an ALLOWLIST - ignore everything, then re-include the few paths the
# build reads. A denylist would have to be extended every time the repo grows a
# directory, and the cost of forgetting is silent: the context here is 3.1 GB
# unfiltered (ios/.build alone is 2 GB, .git 533 MB, the OCR corpus 152 MB), and
# every byte is uploaded to the daemon on every build.
*

# The backend sources, and only the sources.
!backend/Tankbook.slnx
!backend/src/

# Embedded by the csproj at build time: the canonical payload schemas that
# migration 002 inserts into payload_schemas. Not optional - restore fails
# without them.
!docs/schemas/

# Never worth sending even from inside the allowed paths: build output, and the
# gitignored runtime config whose committed *.template.json sibling is what the
# image renders instead (a real appsettings.json here would bake a developer's
# local credentials into the image).
backend/src/**/bin/
backend/src/**/obj/
backend/src/Tankbook.Api/appsettings.json
backend/src/Tankbook.Api/appsettings.Development.json
